From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: supply: mt6375-charger: add the connector protection

The stock charger framework of the Lenovo TB375FC watches a sensor at the
USB connector and raises a GPIO when that gets too hot. Describe the sensor
by the name of its thermal zone, and the GPIO.

---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml
index 0b149d87a0b14e904ac3dc76862579c5c73c4965..4eba260a2770b894b01544ae9e86021ae33586ed 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/mediatek,mt6375-charger.yaml
@@ -39,6 +39,19 @@ properties:
       The power supply of the USB port controller, which tells how much current
       the port can give. Without it the input stays at the USB default.
 
+  mediatek,connector-thermal-zone:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+    description:
+      The name of the thermal zone of the sensor at the USB connector. While
+      that cannot be read the input stays at the USB default. When it reads too
+      hot charging stops and the input goes down until it has cooled down.
+
+  mediatek,vbus-protect-gpios:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      What the board has to protect VBUS when the USB connector gets too hot.
+      It is asserted for as long as that lasts.
+
   usb-otg-vbus-regulator:
     type: object
     $ref: /schemas/regulator/regulator.yaml#
